  "name": "Skica in letnice",
  "idea": "Every Lesnik piece begins as a drawing made together at the client's table and ends as oak, walnut or larch from the Poljanska dolina sawmills, so the page is a joiner's working sheet: dimension lines measure the type, and woodcut-printed end-grain cross-sections of the three woods are the only pictures.",
