  "pairing": "fraunces-source-sans",
  "typeCharacter": "Fraunces in its heavy, soft-cornered optical display weight feels carved and warm without being nostalgic; it sets the h1 very large (about 8vw) in sentence case and the section titles at 48 to 64 px, always upright, while Source Sans 3 carries the leads at 20 px, the body at 17 px and the cutting-list rows at 22 px semibold, all sentence case with no tracking tricks.",
  "composition": "Hero on the cool light tint #f2f4f1: columns 1 to 7 hold the h1 in Fraunces heavy #1f1a16 across three lines, with a thin #1f1a16 drafting dimension line (short end ticks, small arrowheads, no numbers) running exactly the width of the first line just above it; below, the lead in Source Sans at 6 columns and one rectangular rust #8a3b1e button with square corners. Columns 8 to 12 hold a large woodcut print of an oak log's end grain, bleeding off the right edge. Under the hero, a full-width rust #8a3b1e ribbon lists the six offerings in Source Sans semibold #f4f1ec, separated by small square dots. Services: on the tint, title at left over columns 1 to 4 with the price note under it; columns 5 to 12 are a cutting list, one row per offering divided by #c3c8c1 hairlines, the offering name in Source Sans semibold and on the Kuhinje row the waiting-time note in #55524c; a small ink line drawing of a dovetail joint sits in the left column below the note. Story on a full-width walnut #2a1f18 field: title and text in #eee8df across columns 1 to 6, the grandfather and Jaka Lesnik facts as a short paragraph; columns 7 to 12 hold three end-grain woodcut prints of oak, walnut and larch at deliberately different sizes, staggered vertically, each labelled with the wood name below in #d08a45. Steps on the tint: title at columns 1 to 5, then one long dimension line across columns 1 to 12 with three tick points, a step word in Fraunces under each tick (narišemo, izdelamo, montiramo) and a short Source Sans line beneath, no numbers. Call on the rust #8a3b1e field: question in Fraunces #f4f1ec at columns 1 to 6, the phone number as a huge Fraunces numeral spanning columns 7 to 12, and the invitation line under it. Contact on the tint: address and email at columns 1 to 4, a simple schematic line map of Kidričeva cesta at columns 5 to 8 in #1f1a16 lines with one rust marker, opening hours as a week strip at columns 9 to 12.",
  "imagery": "No photographs anywhere. The art is woodcut-style relief prints in dense ink of tree end grain: oak (tight rings, medullary rays), walnut (wide wavy rings), larch (sharp contrasting rings), each on a plain flat ground, cut out as a labelled AI picture: oak in the hero on the light tint #f2f4f1 in ink #1f1a16, the three woods together on walnut #2a1f18 printed in #eee8df with the larch touched with #d08a45. Plus thin ink line drawings: a dovetail joint (services) and drafting dimension lines used as dividers. No furniture is drawn, so nothing stands in for the client's own work.",
  "signature": "Drafting dimension lines with end ticks that measure the headline and carry the three steps, set against big woodcut end-grain prints of oak, walnut and larch, as if the client's sketch and the sawmill log share the same sheet.",
  "copy": {
    "headline": "Pohištvo iz masivnega lesa, narisano za vaš dom",
    "lead": "Kuhinje, vgradne omare, mize, postelje, stopnice in notranja vrata. Vsak kos narišemo skupaj z vami, izdelamo v delavnici v Škofji Loki in ga sami montiramo."
  },
  "imagePrompt": "One flat full-page screenshot of a desktop website homepage, 1536×1024 px, no browser window, no device frame, no perspective, straight-on. No photographs at all; the only pictures are woodcut relief prints and thin ink line drawings. Page ground is a cool very light grey-green tint #f2f4f1 (not cream). Text ink #1f1a16, muted text #55524c, hairlines #c3c8c1. Headings in Fraunces, heavy soft-cornered display weight, sentence case, upright, never italic; body in Source Sans 3. Layout on a 12-column grid, left-aligned, generous margins. HERO: columns 1-7, a very large three-line Fraunces heavy headline in #1f1a16; directly above its first line a thin technical drafting dimension line with small end ticks and arrowheads spanning exactly that line's width, with no numbers. Below it the lead in Source Sans 20 px across six columns, then a single rectangular square-cornered button filled rust #8a3b1e with light #f4f1ec label. Columns 8-12: a large woodcut print of an oak log's end-grain cross-section, tight growth rings, radial medullary rays and bark edge, carved black ink #1f1a16 on the plain tint ground, bleeding off the right page edge, no text inside. Under the hero a full-width rust #8a3b1e ribbon with a single line of short offering words in Source Sans semibold #f4f1ec separated by small square dots. SERVICES on the tint: section title in Fraunces at columns 1-4 with a short muted note beneath and a small thin ink line drawing of a dovetail wood joint below it on the plain ground; columns 5-12 a cutting-list table, one row per offering, separated by hairlines #c3c8c1, names in Source Sans semibold 22 px, one row with an extra muted note. STORY: full-width deep walnut field #2a1f18; columns 1-6 title in Fraunces and paragraphs in #eee8df; columns 7-12 three woodcut end-grain prints (oak with tight rings, walnut with wide wavy rings, larch with sharp contrasting rings) printed in light #eee8df on the walnut ground, the larch with touches of #d08a45, at three different sizes staggered up and down, each with a small wood-name caption in #d08a45 beneath. STEPS on the tint: title at columns 1-5, then one long thin drafting dimension line spanning all 12 columns with three tick marks; under each tick a short Fraunces word and one line of Source Sans text; no numbers, no icons, no cards. CALL: full-width rust #8a3b1e field; columns 1-6 a Fraunces question in #f4f1ec; columns 7-12 the phone number as a huge Fraunces numeral in #f4f1ec with one short line beneath; no button here. CONTACT on the tint: columns 1-4 address and email in Source Sans; columns 5-8 a simple schematic street map in thin #1f1a16 lines with one small rust #8a3b1e square marker; columns 9-12 opening hours as a seven-day week strip with hairline dividers. Flat colour only: no gradients, no shadows, no glass effects, no pill shapes, no icons, no emoji, no people, no faces, no hands, no furniture drawings, no photos, no logos."
}

